{"name":"Blue Lips","hex":"#a6bce2","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"},{"term":"lips","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of lip"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of lip"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lips"}],"entries":[{"title":"Blue Lips (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Blue Lips is a 2018 short film co-produced, co-written and starring Swedish singer-songwriter Tove Lo. The film was released on YouTube and Vevo on 19 October 2018, and features ten songs, nine from Lo's third studio album, Blue Lips (2017), and one from her second studio album, Lady Wood (2016). It was directed and written by Malia James with Lo working on the screenplay as well while Nathan Scherrer and Laura Haber served as executive producers."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/5f/Blue_Lips_poster.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue_Lips_(film)","wikidata":"Q58814988"},{"title":"Blue Lips (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Blue Lips\" is a single by American experimental rock band Bear Hands featuring backing vocals from Ursula Rose."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/71/Bear_Hands_Blue_Lips.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue_Lips_(song)","wikidata":"Q65085501"},{"title":"Blue Lips (Tove Lo album)","blocks":[{"text":"Blue Lips is the third studio album by Swedish singer Tove Lo. It was released on 17 November 2017 by Island Records. Blue Lips is considered the second half of a two-piece concept album that describe \"highs, lows and ultimate demise of a relationship.\" Its chapters \"Light Beams\" and \"Pitch Black\" succeed the chapters \"Fairy Dust\" and \"Fire Fade\" from her previous album Lady Wood (2016)."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/e5/Tove_Lo_-_Blue_Lips.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue_Lips_(Tove_Lo_album)","wikidata":"Q39045338"},{"title":"Lip","blocks":[{"text":"The lips are a horizontal pair of soft appendages attached to the jaws and are the most visible part of the mouth of many animals, including humans. Mammal lips are soft, movable and serve to facilitate the ingestion of food and the articulation of sound and speech. Human lips are also a somatosensory organ, and can be an erogenous zone when used in kissing and other acts of intimacy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/Lips_2023.jpg/330px-Lips_2023.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lip","wikidata":"Q15173"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/5/59/BlueLipsDeluxeVinylCover.png/250px-BlueLipsDeluxeVinylCover.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/59/BlueLipsDeluxeVinylCover.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/5/59/BlueLipsDeluxeVinylCover.png/250px-BlueLipsDeluxeVinylCover.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABlueLipsDeluxeVinylCover.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/Mou